    93	A CNF formula $\phi$ is \emph{monotone} if the literals of each clause $c_i$  are either all positive, or all negative.
    94	The so-called \emph{negative clauses} contain only negative literals while \emph{positive clauses} contain only positive literals. 
    95	
    96	A CNF formula $\phi$ is \emph{monotone planar} if there exists a variable-cycle $\pi$ such that the variable-clause graph $\inciGraphSign{\phi, \pi}$ 
    97	has a planar embedding in which %
    98	positive clause nodes are inside (\resp outside) the curve formed by the variable cycle, while negative clauses nodes are outside (\resp inside).
    99	
   100	\MPTSAT asks: given a monotone planar 3-CNF formula $\phi$, a cycle $\pi$, a planar embedding of $\inciGraphSign{\phi, \pi}$, is $\phi$ satisfiable?
   101	This problem is \npc~\cite{de2010optimal}.
