STEP 0 points to a cleaner family than the initial “random planted 3-SAT” hypothesis. The paper itself supplies a certificate-preserving transformation (Theorem 3.2), while the resulting generated subclass is 2-CNF and therefore has a linear-time implication-graph algorithm. I’m treating it as Track B, not claiming distributional NP-hardness: the benchmark gap is between mechanically traversing a 504-node implication graph and recognizing a quadratic-residue pattern that reconstructs the planted assignment compactly.
