Implemented and verified a Track A generator based on the paper’s Section 7.1 NCL-to-Linear-Literal-Planar-3-SAT reconfiguration reduction and PSPACE-completeness theorem ([paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.14713)).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2506_14713.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.14713/gen_2506_14713.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.14713/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.14713/README.md)
- [bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.14713/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.14713/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.14713/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Key results:

- All G1–G9 gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Memoized A*: 800,000 states and 153.37 seconds across eight attempts.
- Bare oracle: 0/3 solved.
- Structural hint: 0/3 solved.
- Placebo hint: 0/3 solved.
- Shipping answer: 160 elements, 576 characters.
- Emission validation: 20/20 instances verified, 20 distinct canonical keys, zero duplicates.

The generated artifact is [2506.14713.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/artifacts/2506.14713.jsonl). Temporary paper downloads and isolated G9 working directories were moved to the recoverable desktop trash.
